  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "A private preflight authorizes or refreshes Epic Sandbox access without exposing credentials, codes, or tokens in source control, chat, browser output, normal logs, reports, or ordinary UI.",
    "The recorded journey reaches an already-connected Camila staff record without displaying Epic authentication.",
    "OAuth state, nonce, issuer, redirect, transaction, scope, expiry, refresh rotation, encryption, revocation, and redaction controls pass targeted tests and security review.",
    "Camila's staff record shows only facts returned by enabled R4 Read/Search APIs or the versioned last-known-good snapshot, with per-item provenance.",
    "A successful refresh publishes a complete snapshot atomically; partial or failed refreshes never combine old and new fields under a Live label.",
    "Live failure serves the prior complete snapshot only as Snapshot fallback with its original synchronization time; no snapshot produces Unavailable.",
    "Patient, caregiver, transportation, public, search, export, log, and accessible-text projections exclude Epic-only clinical fields.",
    "Only Camila is Epic-backed, non-Camila fixtures trigger no Epic request, and all Epic operations remain read-only.",
    "The UI provides accessible loading, empty, partial-source, unauthorized, expiry, rate/error, fallback, and unavailable states without unsupported partnership, production, or writeback claims."
  ],
